  "id": "internal-locus-of-control",
  "term": "internal locus of control",
  "definition": "Internal locus of control is a person’s general expectation that what happens in life depends mainly on their own actions, choices, abilities, or effort rather than on outside forces. It is described as a relatively stable style of explaining outcomes that affects thinking, emotions, and behavior.",
